      "writtenOn": "2023-06-09T09:15:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e what other configs are enabled when setting XEN\u003dy?\n\nWith the latest patch, below configs are enabled:\n\nCONFIG_XEN_DOM0\u003dy\nCONFIG_XEN\u003dy\nCONFIG_XEN_BLKDEV_FRONTEND\u003dy\nCONFIG_XEN_NETDEV_FRONTEND\u003dy\nCONFIG_HVC_XEN\u003dy\nCONFIG_HVC_XEN_FRONTEND\u003dy\nCONFIG_XEN_XENBUS_FRONTEND\u003dy\nCONFIG_SWIOTLB_XEN\u003dy\nCONFIG_XEN_EFI\u003dy\nCONFIG_XEN_AUTO_XLATE\u003dy\n\n\u003e What is the impact on kernel memory size?\n\nFor the kernel\u0027s static size, below are detailed increasing number for some sections.\n\n.text section: +0x20000\n.rodata: +0x8520\n.BTF: +0xC570\n.data.percpu: +0x3c0\n.data: +0x14C0\n.bss: +0x1E40\n\n\nThe ELF section log with disabling XEN: https://termbin.com/3iwh\nThe ELF section log with enabling XEN: https://termbin.com/3opw\n\n\nI think you might have concern for using extra memory after enabling Xen config, especially when we run Android on Cuttlefish VM (QEMU based), blow is the log for /proc/meminfo.\n\nWithout Xen config:\n\n```\nvsoc_arm64_only:/ # cat /proc/meminfo                                          \nMemTotal:        4015684 kB\nMemFree:         1020600 kB\nMemAvailable:    2471468 kB\nBuffers:            4148 kB\nCached:          1712252 kB\nSwapCached:            0 kB\nActive:          1573032 kB\nInactive:         926468 kB\nActive(anon):     824056 kB\nInactive(anon):      928 kB\nActive(file):     748976 kB\nInactive(file):   925540 kB\nUnevictable:       42904 kB\nMlocked:           10392 kB\nSwapTotal:             0 kB\nSwapFree:              0 kB\nDirty:               880 kB\nWriteback:             0 kB\nAnonPages:        826012 kB\nMapped:           638124 kB\nShmem:             38156 kB\nKReclaimable:     101224 kB\nSlab:             227344 kB\nSReclaimable:     101224 kB\nSUnreclaim:       126120 kB\nKernelStack:       29376 kB\nShadowCallStack:    7352 kB\nPageTables:        94300 kB\nSecPageTables:         0 kB\nNFS_Unstable:          0 kB\nBounce:               