      "message": "\u003e Does it really need to be in the android-mainline tree? \n\nI think the question could be converted to: does Google want to support Xen virtualization for Android Car building?  If this is in Google\u0027s longterm plan, then android-mainline tree is the best place to land this patch.\n\nI would like to leave this question to @Alistair Delva, essentially, it would be best if what I am doing can match with Google\u0027s strategy.\n\n\u003e Couldn\u0027t that be added downstream of android-mainline?\n\nGood point.  Though my ambition is to add change to the android-mainline tree 😊, I hope the community can directly download the latest code base for building Android and kernel images with support Xen.\n\nIf finally we veto the solution either adding change to gki_defconfig or adding a new Xen build config in android-mainline, then downstream would be a good option for adding patch.  At least, we have a public repository to tell developers they can try it.\n\nTo be clear, here \"downstream\" means a stable kernel branch (e.g. aosp/android15-6.1), right?",
