      "writtenOn": "2023-06-13T06:49:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e And again, Xen is \"legacy\" technology, no new devices should really\n\u003e be using it, and especially on ARM64 platforms, where Xen really\n\u003e isn\u0027t a solidly supported platform upstream (i.e. there have not\n\u003e been any upstream arm64 xen changes in the kernel in years).\n\u003e Are you sure it even works? 😊\n\nA challenge question 😜.  So, yes, I can confirm Xen works on aarch64 and can boot up successfully with the latest Linux kernel.  In Linaro we have a distro named \"Trusted substract reference\" (TRS) which supports Xen by default and we do CI/CD testing daily for it [1].\n\nI will deliver a session for updating current status for porting Android automotive on Xen in next week (20th, June), and in the session we will show a demo for booting Android automotive OS on Xen virtual machine (with enabling virtio-gpu!).  I will make sure all of you will receive the invitation and share the slides with you.\n\n[1] https://trs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/manual/feature.html#virtualization",
      "parentUuid": "23f8a276_d511ba45",
      "revId": "61214567014ac28d87c837ec69cae43134d90f42",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1526db39_f51891ab",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2068522
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T19:21:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Greg: Xen is not legacy. Xen is widely used today in *new* embedded and automotive deployments. At AMD/Xilinx alone we have several new Xen deployments both ARM and x86, both embedded (5G antennas, industrial grade screwdrivers, robots, etc.) and automotive (IVI, ADAS). The automotive customers typically run Android on top of Xen. My Xen team at AMD/Xilinx has grown from just me to 6 people in the last 3 years and our team\u0027s purpose is only to support Xen for embedded/automotive.",
      "parentUuid": "0a7271b7_029be945",
      "revId": "61214567014ac28d87c837ec69cae43134d90f42",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fea32164_5cd3c321",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
